# Committed defaults loaded by `expo start` (NODE_ENV=development).
# APP_ENV defaults to "local", so the app targets your machine's API.
#
# You normally don't edit this file: `npm start` auto-writes your LAN IP into
# .env.local (gitignored) via scripts/sync-local-env.js. See .env.example for
# every supported variable (Google SSO, custom API URL, etc.).
